{"name":"Vertigo Cherry","hex":"#990055","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"vertigo","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sensation of whirling and loss of balance, caused by looking down from a great height or by disease affecting the inner ear.","A disordered or imbalanced state of mind or things analogous to physical vertigo; mental giddiness or dizziness."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vertigo"},{"term":"cherry","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small fruit, usually red, black or yellow, with a smooth hard seed and a short hard stem.","Prunus subg. Cerasus, trees or shrubs that bear cherries."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Containing or having the taste of cherries.","Of a bright red color; cherry red."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cherry"}],"entries":[{"title":"Vertigo","blocks":[{"text":"Vertigo is a condition in which a person has the sensation that they are moving, or that objects around them are moving, when that is not the case. Often it feels like a spinning or swaying movement. It may be associated with nausea, vomiting, perspiration, or difficulties walking. It is typically worse when the head is moved. Vertigo is the most common type of dizziness."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/3D_still_showing_Vertigo.jpg/330px-3D_still_showing_Vertigo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vertigo"},{"title":"Cherry","blocks":[{"text":"A cherry is the fruit of many plants of the genus Prunus, and is a fleshy drupe."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Cherry_season_%2848216568227%29.jpg/330px-Cherry_season_%2848216568227%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cherry"},{"title":"Cerise (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Cerise is a dark pink shade."}],"image":"https://t